&lt;h1&gt;


Adding Real‑Time IP Communication Status to the TV Inventory Dashboard
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I extended the Prisma schema and React UI to surface a boolean “IP Comm” flag for each TV device, letting the inventory table show live connectivity status. The change required a new column, type updates, a badge component, and a small store tweak—all done without breaking existing queries.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our inventory page lists hundreds of TV devices, but we had no way to tell if a TV was currently reachable over the network. The backend periodically ingests a CSV report (&lt;code&gt;sis_report.csv&lt;/code&gt;) that contains a &lt;code&gt;terminalAddress&lt;/code&gt; (MAC) and a boolean &lt;code&gt;ip_comm&lt;/code&gt; indicating whether the TV responded to a ping test. The UI displayed a “—” for that column because the Prisma model &lt;code&gt;TvDevice&lt;/code&gt; didn’t have a matching field, resulting in a runtime error:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;TypeError: Cannot read property 'ipComm' of undefined
at InventoryTable (src/features/inventory/InventoryTable.tsx:42:27)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The missing field also meant we couldn’t filter or sort by connectivity status, limiting our ability to quickly isolate offline units.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first attempt was to compute the IP status on the client side by joining the CSV data with the fetched devices in &lt;code&gt;useDevicesStore&lt;/code&gt;. I added a helper &lt;code&gt;calcIpComm(devices, csvRows)&lt;/code&gt; that returned a map of MAC → boolean. Then I patched each &lt;code&gt;TvDeviceRow&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;ipComm&lt;/code&gt; before rendering.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Problems:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Performance hit&lt;/strong&gt; – The CSV can be &amp;gt;10 k rows; parsing it on every page load caused a noticeable UI lag (&amp;gt;500 ms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Stale data&lt;/strong&gt; – The CSV is refreshed by a separate cron job; the client‑side merge never updated until a full page reload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Type mismatch&lt;/strong&gt; – The &lt;code&gt;TvDeviceRow&lt;/code&gt; interface in &lt;code&gt;use-devices-store.ts&lt;/code&gt; didn’t have an &lt;code&gt;ipComm&lt;/code&gt; field, so TypeScript threw errors across the codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I reverted that approach and decided to push the IP flag into the database so the UI could treat it like any other column.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Extend the Prisma schema
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;File: &lt;code&gt;prisma/schema.prisma&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -49,6 +49,13 @@&lt;/span&gt; model TvDevice {
tvPowerOns7Days  Int?
stateModified    DateTime?
&lt;span class="err"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  // IP communication status – derived from the SIS report (MAC ↔ ip_comm)
+  // Null means we haven’t processed a report for this device yet.
+  ipComm           Boolean?   @default(null)
+  ipCommCheckedAt  DateTime?  @default(null)
&lt;/span&gt; }
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Why Boolean?&lt;/em&gt; The SIS report only tells us “reachable” (&lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt;) or “not reachable” (&lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;). Using &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; signals “unknown” – useful for newly added TVs that haven’t been scanned yet.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After the schema change I ran:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx prisma migrate dev &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--name&lt;/span&gt; add-ip-comm-status
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Prisma generated the migration SQL:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight sql"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;ALTER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;TABLE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"TvDevice"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;ADD&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;COLUMN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"ipComm"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;BOOLEAN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;ALTER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;TABLE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"TvDevice"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;ADD&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;COLUMN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"ipCommCheckedAt"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;TIMESTAMP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


2. Update the TypeScript store
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;File: &lt;code&gt;src/hooks/use-devices-store.ts&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -21,6 +21,8 @@&lt;/span&gt; export interface TvDeviceRow {
chromecastState: string | null;
stays60Days: number | null;
tvPowerOns7Days: number | null;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  ipComm: boolean | null;
+  ipCommCheckedAt: string | null;
&lt;/span&gt; }
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The store pulls rows via &lt;code&gt;prisma.tvDevice.findMany()&lt;/code&gt;. Adding the fields required no extra code because Prisma automatically includes them in the generated type.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Create a badge component for IP status
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;File: &lt;code&gt;src/components/inventory/status-badge.tsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;IpCommBadge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;variant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"neutral"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;—&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;variant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"success"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Online&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;variant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"danger"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Offline&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Badge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I kept the UI consistent with existing badges (&lt;code&gt;OccupiedBadge&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;OutOfServiceBadge&lt;/code&gt;). The component returns a neutral dash for unknown status, mirroring the rest of the table.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


4. Wire the badge into the inventory table
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;File: &lt;code&gt;src/features/inventory/InventoryTable.tsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@&lt;/span&gt; import {
SerialBadge,
OutOfServiceBadge,
OccupiedBadge,
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  IpCommBadge,
&lt;/span&gt; } from "@/components/inventory/status-badge";
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then inside the row rendering loop:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;td&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"px-4 py-2"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;IpCommBadge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;row&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;td&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I also added a column header:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;th&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"px-4 py-2 text-left"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;IP Comm&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;th&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


5. Populate the new columns from the SIS report
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The backend job that processes &lt;code&gt;sis_report.csv&lt;/code&gt; already runs nightly. I extended its parser (&lt;code&gt;src/jobs/process-sis-report.ts&lt;/code&gt;) to upsert the &lt;code&gt;ipComm&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ipCommCheckedAt&lt;/code&gt; fields:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tvDevice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;upsert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;terminalAddress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;mac&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipCommFlag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;ipCommCheckedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;terminalAddress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;mac&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// other required fields...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ipCommFlag&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;ipCommCheckedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Because the fields are optional, existing rows are updated without a migration lock, and newly discovered devices receive the flag immediately.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


6. Adjust the API response shape
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our GraphQL resolver (&lt;code&gt;src/graphql/resolvers/tvDevice.ts&lt;/code&gt;) now includes &lt;code&gt;ipComm&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ipCommCheckedAt&lt;/code&gt; in the selection set:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tvDevice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findMany&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;ipComm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;ipCommCheckedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// …other fields&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No client‑side changes were needed beyond the badge import.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Key Takeaway
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Never treat a missing column as a UI‑only problem; push the data into the source of truth.&lt;/strong&gt; Adding a boolean flag to the Prisma model gave us a single source of truth, eliminated client‑side merging, and let us reuse existing type‑generation pipelines. The pattern—extend the schema, run a migration, update the store interface, and add a small UI component—scales cleanly for any new telemetry field.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What's Next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I plan to add a &lt;strong&gt;real‑time WebSocket&lt;/strong&gt; subscription that pushes &lt;code&gt;ipComm&lt;/code&gt; updates as soon as the SIS job finishes, so the badge flips from “—” to “Online/Offline” without a page refresh. This will involve:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adding a &lt;code&gt;pubsub.publish('IP_COMM_UPDATED', device)&lt;/code&gt; call in the job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposing a GraphQL subscription resolver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Updating &lt;code&gt;InventoryTable&lt;/code&gt; to listen via &lt;code&gt;useSubscription&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That will close the loop between data ingestion and UI responsiveness.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tags:&lt;/em&gt; #vibecoding #buildinpublic #typescript #react #prisma #nextjs #graphql #webdev&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part of my &lt;a href="https://dev.to/zaerohell"&gt;Build in Public&lt;/a&gt; series — sharing the real process of building SaaS projects from Playa del Carmen, México.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Repo: &lt;code&gt;zaerohell/tvview&lt;/code&gt; · 2026-10-12&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;#playadev #buildinpublic&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A cache key describes a task's inputs at one moment. If an input changes&lt;br&gt;
while the command runs, the output may have been built from bytes the key&lt;br&gt;
does not describe. Save it under that key and a later hit restores an&lt;br&gt;
output that matches neither version of the file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It happens more than it sounds: you save a file while a build runs, a&lt;br&gt;
code generator in another task rewrites a shared file, or a tool rewrites&lt;br&gt;
its own config. We read each tool's source, at the version named, to see&lt;br&gt;
what it does after the command exits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


Turborepo 2.11.7
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Turborepo computes the task hash before the task runs. After a&lt;br&gt;
successful run, &lt;code&gt;save_outputs&lt;/code&gt; globs the declared outputs and stores them&lt;br&gt;
under that same hash. It does not look at the inputs again.&lt;br&gt;
Source: &lt;a href="https://github.com/vercel/turborepo/blob/v2.11.7/crates/turborepo-run-cache/src/lib.rs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;crates/turborepo-run-cache/src/lib.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;save_outputs&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


Nx 23.3.0
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nx hashes a task in &lt;code&gt;processTask&lt;/code&gt; before it is scheduled, and after the&lt;br&gt;
run &lt;code&gt;postRunSteps&lt;/code&gt; calls &lt;code&gt;cache.put(task.hash, …)&lt;/code&gt; with that hash. It&lt;br&gt;
does not compare inputs before and after. In batch mode, a task whose&lt;br&gt;
inputs include its dependencies' outputs is hashed again after it runs,&lt;br&gt;
against the files as they are then.&lt;br&gt;
Source: &lt;code&gt;nx@23.3.0&lt;/code&gt;,&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://unpkg.com/nx@23.3.0/dist/src/tasks-runner/task-orchestrator.js" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;dist/src/tasks-runner/task-orchestrator.js&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;code&gt;processTask&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;postRunSteps&lt;/code&gt;) and&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://unpkg.com/nx@23.3.0/dist/src/tasks-runner/cache.js" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;cache.js&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;code&gt;put&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


Vite Task (vite-plus 1.1.0)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vite Task traces the files a task opens (its &lt;code&gt;fspy&lt;/code&gt; tracer) and checks&lt;br&gt;
them after the run. If the task wrote a file it also read, the entry is&lt;br&gt;
not saved and the reason is &lt;code&gt;InputModified&lt;/code&gt;. The check covers reads the&lt;br&gt;
tracer saw from the task's own processes, not the globbed inputs; its&lt;br&gt;
comment notes that a task writing a globbed file it never read gets&lt;br&gt;
repeated misses rather than a wrong entry.&lt;br&gt;
Source: vite-plus 1.1.0 pins vite-task at&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://github.com/voidzero-dev/vite-task/blob/7d69d6577ecf6bd83deee32186de59918a712873/crates/vt/src/session/execute/cache_update.rs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;7d69d65&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;crates/vt/src/session/execute/cache_update.rs&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


vx
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;vx takes the key just before the command and, after it exits, checks&lt;br&gt;
every declared input once, whoever wrote it: the task, your editor, or&lt;br&gt;
another task. Any file written after its digest was learned counts as&lt;br&gt;
moved, even if its bytes are back to the original, because an edit&lt;br&gt;
that was undone mid-run cannot be told apart from no edit at all. A&lt;br&gt;
moved input keeps the run's result, saves no entry, and names the file;&lt;br&gt;
every task downstream skips its save too.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;[vx] app#build: `packages/app/src/routes.gen.ts` changed after its key was taken — the result stands, but is not saved under a key that no longer describes it; if the task writes it, declare it in cache.outputs
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;How strict this is, is yours to choose with &lt;code&gt;cache.inputStability&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;'mutable'&lt;/code&gt; saves when the bytes end identical (for a tool that rewrites&lt;br&gt;
its own &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;code&gt;'unchecked'&lt;/code&gt; turns the check off, and&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;severity: 'error'&lt;/code&gt; fails the task instead of warning.&lt;br&gt;
Source: &lt;code&gt;packages/vx/src/orchestrator/execute-task.ts&lt;/code&gt;; the full story is&lt;br&gt;
in &lt;a href="https://vznjs.github.io/vx/blog/inputs-that-move/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;When an input moves mid-run&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Side by side
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;After the command exits&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Turborepo 2.11.7&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Nx 23.3.0&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Vite Task 1.1.0&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;vx&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Inputs looked at again&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;no&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;no (batch: rehash)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;files the task opened&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;every declared input&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Writes it notices&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the task's own&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;any process's&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;What it does on a change&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;saves&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;saves&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;skips the save&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;skips the save, names file&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Can be relaxed per task&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;n/a&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;n/a&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;n/a&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;inputStability&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The trade
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Checking costs something. vx pays one &lt;code&gt;lstat&lt;/code&gt; per input after a run that&lt;br&gt;
saves, and a task that touches its own inputs rebuilds next time unless&lt;br&gt;
you tell vx how to judge it. Turborepo and Nx skip that work. Vite Task&lt;br&gt;
checks what its tracer already recorded. None of these is free, and&lt;br&gt;
which trade fits depends on how often your inputs move under a running&lt;br&gt;
task.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We chose to make a cache entry mean exactly what its declared inputs say,&lt;br&gt;
and to make the strictness a setting. vx is at&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://vznjs.github.io/vx/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;vznjs.github.io/vx&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on the &lt;a href="https://vznjs.github.io/vx/blog/an-input-moves-four-tools/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;vx blog&lt;/a&gt;. vx is open-source (MIT) task orchestration with a build cache: &lt;a href="https://vznjs.github.io/vx/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;vznjs.github.io/vx&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/vznjs/vx" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Written with AI assistance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every website form should do four things the second someone hits submit: validate the lead, save it somewhere you will actually look, notify you instantly, and reply to the human. Most forms do one of these. Here is a workflow that does all four, and you can steal the whole thing below.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Access
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Download it from my &lt;a href="https://github.com/realtouseef/free-lead-capture-lite" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What it does
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A webhook receives the form POST. An IF node checks the email exists. Good leads get appended to Google Sheets, you get an email with the details, and the lead gets an auto-reply. Bad submissions get a clean 400 response instead of silently rotting in a database.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Build it (10 minutes)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Webhook trigger.&lt;/strong&gt; Add a Webhook node, POST method, path &lt;code&gt;lead-capture&lt;/code&gt;. Set response mode to "Respond to Webhook" so you control the reply.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Validate.&lt;/strong&gt; Add an IF node: string &lt;code&gt;{{ $json.email }}&lt;/code&gt; exists. This one check kills 90% of junk.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Log it.&lt;/strong&gt; Google Sheets node, Append operation, map &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;email&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;phone&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;message&lt;/code&gt;, plus &lt;code&gt;created_at&lt;/code&gt; set to &lt;code&gt;{{ $now.toISO() }}&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;status&lt;/code&gt; set to &lt;code&gt;new&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Notify yourself.&lt;/strong&gt; Gmail node to your own address. Subject: &lt;code&gt;{{ 'New lead: ' + ($json.name || $json.email) }}&lt;/code&gt;. Body: the fields, plain text, scannable in 5 seconds on a phone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Auto-reply.&lt;/strong&gt; Gmail node to &lt;code&gt;{{ $json.email }}&lt;/code&gt;. Keep it short: thanks, we reply within one business day.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Respond.&lt;/strong&gt; Two Respond to Webhook nodes: 200 with a thank-you on the true branch, 400 with "Missing required field: email" on the false branch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The one pattern that makes this maintainable
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Put a Set node right after the trigger and call it CONFIG. Every value the buyer (or future you) might change, your email, the sheet ID, the reply text, lives there as named fields. Downstream nodes reference &lt;code&gt;{{ $('CONFIG').item.json.owner_email }}&lt;/code&gt;. One node to edit, zero hunting through the canvas six months later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Test before you activate
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep it inactive, hit Execute Workflow, and POST test data with curl:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-X&lt;/span&gt; POST &amp;lt;your-webhook-url&amp;gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-H&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Content-Type: application/json'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;-d&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'{"name":"Test","email":"test@example.com","message":"hello"}'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Watch every node turn green. Check the sheet row and both emails. Then activate.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;I packaged this workflow plus four more (Stripe failed-payment recovery, blog-to-social repurposer, review request drip, dead-lead reactivation) into a tested template pack with docs and setup checklists. Here's the full set: &lt;a href="https://whop.com/touseef-ur-rehman/agency-automation-essentials/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;5 Production-Ready n8n Workflows&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Anthropic promediaba 2.500 fusiones de código por día en mayo de 2026. Para septiembre, la cifra superó las &lt;a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/redesigning-source-control" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;30.000 fusiones diarias&lt;/a&gt;: un salto que convirtió a Git en el principal cuello de botella de la compañía y la empujó a construir Scion de Anthropic, su sistema de control de versiones propio, en apenas cinco meses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La decisión no fue optimizar Git, sino dejarlo atrás. Casi todos los usuarios del monorepo ya no son personas: son agentes de Claude y trabajos automatizados que están conectados todo el tiempo, algo que el diseño original de Git nunca tuvo en cuenta.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anthropic migró su monorepo completo de Git a Scion, su sistema propio, en cinco meses durante 2026.- Las fusiones diarias pasaron de 2.500 en mayo a más de 30.000 en septiembre de 2026.- Scion asume que todos los clientes están siempre en línea, al revés del diseño descentralizado de Git.- El historial de la rama principal pesa casi 100 GB, y la copia comprimida supera 25 GB.- Solo en CI, la empresa ejecuta unos 25 millones de checkouts de código por día.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Qué es Scion de Anthropic
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Scion de Anthropic es el sistema de control de versiones que la compañía construyó en 2026 para reemplazar a Git en su monorepo. A diferencia de Git, que es descentralizado, Scion asume que el servidor siempre está disponible y que los clientes piden solo los datos que necesitan.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El nombre responde a una idea concreta: tomar lecciones de otros monorepos gigantes, como &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piper_(source_control_system)" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Piper&lt;/a&gt; de Google y &lt;a href="https://sapling-scm.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Sapling&lt;/a&gt; de Meta, pero ajustarlas a un escenario donde los clientes no son laptops de desarrolladores sino flotas de agentes y máquinas efímeras que se conectan, piden datos puntuales y se desconectan. Ahí está la diferencia de fondo con Git: Git se diseñó para que cualquier clon pudiera trabajar sin red; el sistema de Anthropic asume la red como parte del diseño desde el primer día.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Qué pasó
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El 13 de octubre de 2026, Anthropic publicó en su blog de ingeniería el relato completo de la migración. En mayo de ese año, la empresa fusionaba en promedio 2.500 cambios de código por día en su monorepo; para septiembre, ese número superó los &lt;a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/redesigning-source-control" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;30.000 merges diarios&lt;/a&gt;, unas doce veces el volumen de cuatro meses antes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ese crecimiento no vino de contratar más ingenieros, sino de Claude escribiendo, probando y fusionando código de forma autónoma: iterando sobre ciclos de investigación, haciendo micro-optimizaciones y construyendo servicios nuevos sin supervisión constante en cada paso. El cuello de botella dejó de ser programar y pasó a ser toda la infraestructura pensada para escala humana: control de versiones, builds y CI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La respuesta de Anthropic fue construir, en cinco meses, un sistema de control de versiones propio (Scion de Anthropic) y migrar el monorepo completo desde Git. En paralelo, el equipo entregó una superficie de revisión de código llamada Antique, un buscador de código interno, un sistema de permisos para el repositorio y nuevas formas de integrar grandes volúmenes de cambios ya revisados.&lt;br&gt;
El historial de la rama principal del monorepo de Anthropic pesa casi 100 GB.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


Contexto e historia
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Git es un sistema descentralizado: cada clon es un repositorio completo y autónomo, capaz de calcular diffs, leer historial y hacer blame sin conexión a internet. Para la enorme mayoría de proyectos esa sigue siendo la decisión de diseño correcta, y es buena parte de por qué Git se volvió el estándar. El problema de Anthropic es que su monorepo dejó de encajar en ese molde hace tiempo: el historial de la rama principal pesa casi 100 GB, y una copia comprimida del árbol de trabajo supera los 25 GB.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La compañía ya usaba los parches habituales para monorepos gigantes: shallow clones, sparse checkouts, promisor remotes y, sobre todo, cientos de espejos internos de Git más instantáneas (seeds) guardadas en almacenamiento de objetos. En su punto más alto, Anthropic llegó a operar varios cientos de espejos de Git a la vez para repartir la carga. Esos parches ganaron tiempo, pero se volvieron más difíciles de operar a medida que subía la tasa de fusiones: las seeds se alejaban más de la punta de la rama principal entre cada actualización, y mantener funcionando operaciones que dependen del historial, como diff y blame, exigía cada vez más cuidado manual.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El diagnóstico final fue que Anthropic, como casi cualquier empresa, usaba Git como un sistema centralizado con una sola copia autoritativa, cuando casi todos sus clientes (agentes y trabajos automatizados) ya estaban en línea por definición. Las propiedades que hacen a Git excelente para trabajo distribuido y sin conexión eran, en este caso, las mismas que le impedían escalar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


Detalles técnicos: así funciona el reemplazo de Git
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El principio central del nuevo sistema es la asimetría cliente-servidor. En Git, cualquier cliente puede actuar como servidor completo: tiene todo el historial y puede responder cualquier consulta sin red. En el sistema que reemplazó a Git en Anthropic, el servidor es quien responde las preguntas sobre historial de archivos y blame, crea commits y ejecuta merges y rebases. El cliente, en cambio, solo mantiene una caché local de objetos con tamaño acotado, escribe los archivos del working copy en disco, vigila cambios del sistema de archivos y le da al usuario, humano o agente, una forma ergonómica de hablar con el servidor.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight dot"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;flowchart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;TD&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Agente o CI job"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Cliente del VCS"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;B&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;C&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Servidor central"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;D&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Historial y objetos"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;E&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Blame, diff, merge, rebase"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;subgraph&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;Servidor&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;C&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;D&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;E&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Esa asimetría es lo que permite bajar el consumo de red y disco: el cliente calcula poco por sí mismo, pero a cambio necesita muchísima menos información guardada localmente. Anthropic calcula que, si sus &lt;a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/redesigning-source-control" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;25 millones de checkouts diarios&lt;/a&gt; de CI se sirvieran con Git de forma ingenua, clonando el repositorio completo cada vez, el tráfico superaría los 600 petabytes de datos por día. Con el cliente liviano, cada checkout solo pide los archivos y objetos que la tarea puntual necesita.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El otro cambio estructural es que todas las consultas de control de versiones quedan expuestas como API, no solo como comandos de un cliente. Con Git, un job de CI que necesita saber quién modificó una línea por última vez, o cómo se relacionan dos commits, tiene que mantener una copia local del repositorio o depender de una API específica de un proveedor externo. Con el nuevo sistema, esas mismas consultas están disponibles por API, así que en muchos casos un job no necesita repositorio local en absoluto. Esa propiedad habilitó herramientas internas nuevas, como bisect automatizado y reversión de cambios, construidas directamente sobre la API del servidor.&lt;br&gt;
Anthropic operó varios cientos de espejos de Git antes de construir su reemplazo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Impacto y análisis
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El caso de Anthropic es, por ahora, una anomalía: pocas empresas fusionan 30.000 cambios de código al día. Pero la compañía argumenta que el patrón no es exclusivo de ellos. Cualquier organización que deje que Claude o modelos equivalentes escriban y fusionen código de forma autónoma, sin que un humano revise cada línea antes de cada commit, va a chocar antes o después con los mismos límites de diseño de Git: un sistema pensado para que cada desarrollador trabaje offline, en un mundo donde el cliente típico ya es un agente permanentemente conectado.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El sistema de control de versiones de Anthropic no resuelve el problema solo migrando de herramienta. Construirlo exigió, en paralelo y en los mismos cinco meses, rehacer la revisión de código, el buscador interno y el sistema de permisos del repositorio: un rediseño completo de la cadena que va de que Claude escriba un cambio a que ese cambio quede fusionado y auditable en el monorepo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💭 Clave:&lt;/strong&gt; el propio texto de Anthropic lo resume así: Claude fue a la vez la causa del problema, por el volumen de código que genera, y la herramienta que permitió resolverlo rápido, al ayudar a construir un sistema de control de versiones nuevo en cinco meses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La limitación obvia es que este enfoque centralizado tiene un costo. Si el servidor del VCS interno de Anthropic cae, ningún cliente puede operar sin conexión, a diferencia de un repositorio Git clonado localmente. Para un monorepo con cientos de agentes y pipelines de CI dependiendo de ese servidor en todo momento, la disponibilidad del servidor pasa a ser, literalmente, la disponibilidad de poder programar.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Qué sigue
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Anthropic no publicó una fecha para liberar como proyecto abierto el sistema que reemplazó a Git, y nada en el anuncio sugiere que lo vaya a hacer pronto: está hecho a medida para su propio monorepo y su propia escala de uso de agentes. Lo que sí confirmó la empresa es que va a seguir invirtiendo en esta infraestructura, porque la demanda interna de fusionar código es, en sus palabras, prácticamente infinita. Cada cuello de botella que eliminan dispara de inmediato un aumento en la cantidad de código que producen.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El caso vale como referencia para cualquier equipo que esté evaluando cuánto código puede empezar a fusionar un modelo como Claude sin intervención humana directa. Si la tasa de cambios por día se multiplica por doce en cuatro meses, como pasó en Anthropic entre mayo y septiembre de 2026, la pregunta deja de ser qué modelo usar y pasa a ser qué tan rápido se cae la infraestructura de desarrollo detrás de él.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;📖 Resumen en Telegram: &lt;a href="https://telegra.ph/Scion-de-Anthropic-de-2500-a-30000-merges-diarios-10-13" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Ver resumen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Probalo vos: leé el anuncio técnico completo de Anthropic y fijate cuántos de los 25 millones de checkouts diarios que describen se parecen a los de tu propio pipeline de CI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Preguntas frecuentes
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿Qué es el VCS interno de Anthropic y para qué sirve?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Es el sistema de control de versiones que Anthropic construyó para reemplazar a Git en su monorepo principal. Sirve para que agentes de Claude, pipelines de CI y desarrolladores humanos lean, modifiquen y fusionen código sin que cada cliente necesite una copia completa del historial.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿Por qué Anthropic no se quedó con Git?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Porque el diseño descentralizado de Git, pensado para clientes que trabajan offline, dejó de encajar cuando casi todos los clientes del repositorio pasaron a ser agentes y trabajos siempre conectados. Mantener espejos y seeds de Git se volvió más difícil de operar a medida que las fusiones diarias crecieron de 2.500 a más de 30.000.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿Cuánto tardó Anthropic en migrar de Git al nuevo sistema?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cinco meses. En ese mismo período, el equipo también construyó Antique, su superficie de revisión de código, un buscador de código interno y un sistema de permisos para el repositorio.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿En qué se inspiró Scion de Anthropic?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;En proyectos previos de control de versiones a escala de monorepo, como Piper de Google y Sapling de Meta, que ya habían resuelto parte de los mismos problemas de escala para sus propios repositorios gigantes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿Qué pasa si el servidor del sistema de control de versiones de Anthropic falla?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A diferencia de un repositorio Git clonado, donde cada copia local sigue funcionando sin conexión, los clientes de este sistema dependen de que el servidor esté disponible para casi cualquier operación, desde hacer un commit hasta consultar el historial de un archivo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Referencias
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/redesigning-source-control" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Anthropic Engineering&lt;/a&gt;: el anuncio original sobre la migración de Git a Scion de Anthropic, publicado el 13 de octubre de 2026.- &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piper_(source_control_system)" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Wikipedia&lt;/a&gt;: ficha sobre Piper, el sistema de control de versiones interno de Google que inspiró parte del diseño.- &lt;a href="https://sapling-scm.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Sapling&lt;/a&gt;: sitio oficial del sistema de control de versiones de Meta, la otra referencia citada por Anthropic.- &lt;a href="https://git-scm.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Git&lt;/a&gt;: documentación oficial del sistema de control de versiones que Anthropic reemplazó en su monorepo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;📱 &lt;strong&gt;¿Te gusta este contenido?&lt;/strong&gt; Únete a nuestro canal de Telegram &lt;a href="https://t.me/programacion" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;@programacion&lt;/a&gt; donde publicamos a diario lo más relevante de tecnología, IA y desarrollo. Resúmenes rápidos, contenido fresco todos los días.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


Adding Extension and IP Columns to Guest and Office Phones in a Next.js Dashboard
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I extended the Prisma schema and the dashboard UI to expose phone extension and IP address for both Guest and Office phones. The change required schema migration, TypeScript model updates, and a few tweaks in the data‑grid components.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our internal inventory dashboard lists phones by model, serial number, building, etc. Two fields that the facilities team constantly asks for—dialing extension and network IP—were missing from the Guest Phone and Office Phone tables. The UI displayed a “null” placeholder, and the backend had no way to store the data, leading to manual CSV merges that broke the single source of truth.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The symptom was simple: when querying &lt;code&gt;GuestPhone&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;OfficePhone&lt;/code&gt; via Prisma, the &lt;code&gt;ext&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ip&lt;/code&gt; properties were always &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;. The UI component &lt;code&gt;DataGrid&lt;/code&gt; threw a TypeScript error because the &lt;code&gt;Row&lt;/code&gt; interface didn’t contain those keys, and the Prisma client generated type definitions that omitted them entirely.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first instinct was to add the two columns directly in the UI layer, treating them as computed fields that would be filled from an external CSV import. I created a temporary &lt;code&gt;ext&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ip&lt;/code&gt; property inside the React component’s state, hoping to map them later. The approach failed for two reasons:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Type safety broke&lt;/strong&gt; – the generated Prisma types didn’t include the fields, so TypeScript complained whenever I tried to assign them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Persistence was missing&lt;/strong&gt; – without schema changes, the data never persisted to the database, so the UI always reverted to &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; after a refresh.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I rolled back those changes and decided to address the root cause: the database schema.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Extend the Prisma schema
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I opened &lt;code&gt;prisma/schema.prisma&lt;/code&gt; and added two nullable string columns to both &lt;code&gt;GuestPhone&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;OfficePhone&lt;/code&gt;. The diff looks like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -544,6 +544,11 @@&lt;/span&gt; model GuestPhone {
model String?
serialNumber String @unique
building String?
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  // Extensión de marcación ("5" + no. de habitación) e IP — cruzadas desde
+  // el listad
+  ext String?   // e.g., "5123"
+  ip  String?   // e.g., "10.0.2.45"
&lt;/span&gt; }
&lt;span class="err"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt; model OfficePhone {
id          Int      @id @default(autoincrement())
dept        String?
ext         String?   // added
serialNumber String   @unique
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  ip          String?   // added
&lt;/span&gt;   collaboratorNumber String?
}
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Why nullable?&lt;/em&gt; Existing rows don’t have these values yet, so making them optional avoids a migration that would otherwise require default data for every record.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After saving, I ran:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx prisma migrate dev &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--name&lt;/span&gt; add-ext-ip-to-phones
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Prisma generated the migration SQL, added the columns, and updated the client types (&lt;code&gt;@prisma/client&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Update TypeScript interfaces
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The dashboard pages import a local &lt;code&gt;Row&lt;/code&gt; interface to type the data grid rows. I added the new fields in both pages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/app/(dashboard)/guest-phones/page.tsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@&lt;/span&gt; interface Row {
model: string | null;
building: string | null;
serialNumber: string;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  ext: string | null;
+  ip: string | null;
&lt;/span&gt; }
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/app/(dashboard)/office-phones/page.tsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@&lt;/span&gt; interface Row {
dept: string | null;
ext: string | null;
serialNumber: string;
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  ip: string? null;
&lt;/span&gt;   collaboratorNumber: string | null;
}
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Note the small typo I caught during the diff: &lt;code&gt;ip: string? null;&lt;/code&gt; – I corrected it to &lt;code&gt;ip: string | null;&lt;/code&gt; before committing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Adjust the data‑grid column definitions
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both pages use a &lt;code&gt;columns&lt;/code&gt; array for the &lt;code&gt;DataGrid&lt;/code&gt;. I inserted two new columns after the &lt;code&gt;serialNumber&lt;/code&gt; column.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// guest-phones/page.tsx (excerpt)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;headerName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;flex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;building&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;headerName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Building&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;flex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;serialNumber&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;headerName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Serial #&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;flex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;ext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;headerName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Ext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;flex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;renderCell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;ip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;headerName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;IP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;flex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;renderCell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The same pattern was applied to &lt;code&gt;office-phones/page.tsx&lt;/code&gt;. The &lt;code&gt;renderCell&lt;/code&gt; fallback ensures the UI stays clean when values are still &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


4. Populate existing rows (optional script)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since the columns are nullable, the UI works out‑of‑the‑box, but we wanted to seed the data from an existing CSV that the facilities team maintains. I wrote a one‑off script under &lt;code&gt;scripts/seedPhoneMetadata.ts&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PrismaClient&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@prisma/client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;csv&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;csv-parser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;PrismaClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createReadStream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;data/phone-metadata.csv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;pipe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;csv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;serialNumber&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ip&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;guestPhone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;updateMany&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;serialNumber&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ip&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;officePhone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;updateMany&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;serialNumber&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ip&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Metadata seeded&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;finally&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prisma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;$disconnect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Running &lt;code&gt;ts-node scripts/seedPhoneMetadata.ts&lt;/code&gt; filled the new columns for the handful of phones we already had. Future inserts now require &lt;code&gt;ext&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ip&lt;/code&gt; in the payload, but they remain optional.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


5. Verify end‑to‑end
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I refreshed the dashboard, added a new Guest Phone via the “Add” modal (which now includes &lt;code&gt;Ext&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;IP&lt;/code&gt; inputs), and saw the values appear instantly in the grid. The Prisma client generated type definitions now expose &lt;code&gt;ext?: string | null&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ip?: string | null&lt;/code&gt;, so my TypeScript code compiles without any &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt; casts.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Key Takeaway
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When you need to expose new data points in a full‑stack app, &lt;strong&gt;extend the source of truth first&lt;/strong&gt; (the database schema). Adding columns directly in the UI creates a type mismatch and forces you to carry temporary work‑arounds. A single migration, followed by interface updates, keeps the type system happy and guarantees persistence.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What's Next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I plan to add &lt;strong&gt;inline editing&lt;/strong&gt; for the &lt;code&gt;ext&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ip&lt;/code&gt; fields in the data grid, leveraging &lt;code&gt;@tanstack/react-table&lt;/code&gt;’s cell editors. That will let the facilities team update phone metadata without leaving the dashboard, closing the feedback loop entirely.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Roberto Luna Osorio – Full Stack Developer &amp;amp; Project Lead&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Playa del Carmen, México  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


vibecoding #buildinpublic #prisma #nextjs #typescript #react #database-migration
&lt;/h1&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Part of my &lt;a href="https://dev.to/zaerohell"&gt;Build in Public&lt;/a&gt; series — sharing the real process of building SaaS projects from Playa del Carmen, México.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Repo: &lt;code&gt;zaerohell/pcview&lt;/code&gt; · 2026-10-12&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;#playadev #buildinpublic&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


Adding Auth‑Based UI Hiding, Session Cleanup, and Neon/​Vercel Integration to the UHPCM Patch Monitor
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I refactored the front‑end to hide header controls when no user session exists and purge client‑side data on logout, added a proper &lt;code&gt;.gitignore&lt;/code&gt; for Vercel deployments, and wired the app to Neon PostgreSQL via Vercel serverless functions. The changes tighten security, reduce stale state, and make the stack portable between local dev and production.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The original monitor‑parches‑uhpcm repo displayed the full navigation header regardless of authentication state. That meant unauthenticated users could see “Upload”, “Export”, and other actions that should only be available after a successful login.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On logout the client never cleared the in‑memory store, so residual patch data lingered in the UI and could be inadvertently re‑submitted. In production (Vercel) the repo also committed the hidden &lt;code&gt;.vercel&lt;/code&gt; folder, causing noisy diffs and accidental exposure of Vercel’s build cache. Finally, the app only persisted data locally (&lt;code&gt;./data&lt;/code&gt;) and lacked a cloud‑ready database, limiting scalability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Error symptoms:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Uncaught TypeError: cannot read property 'session' of undefined
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;when the UI tried to render controls without a valid session, and stale rows remained visible after &lt;code&gt;session.logout()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first attempt was to sprinkle &lt;code&gt;if (session)&lt;/code&gt; checks around each button’s click handler in &lt;code&gt;public/app.js&lt;/code&gt;. That quickly became a maintenance nightmare—every new control required a duplicate guard. I also tried clearing the global &lt;code&gt;store&lt;/code&gt; object manually in the logout callback, but missed a few nested references, leaving hidden data in the DOM.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the Vercel ignore issue I added &lt;code&gt;/.vercel&lt;/code&gt; to the existing &lt;code&gt;.gitignore&lt;/code&gt;, but the folder was already tracked, so the change had no effect until I removed the folder from history, which was overkill for a simple fix.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. UI Guard at the root level
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of scattering guards, I introduced a single &lt;code&gt;renderHeader()&lt;/code&gt; function that decides which controls to inject based on &lt;code&gt;session.isAuthenticated&lt;/code&gt;. The diff in &lt;code&gt;public/app.js&lt;/code&gt; adds the logic and a small helper to clear the UI on logout.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -210,6 +210,16 @@&lt;/span&gt; function handleErr(e) {
if (e instanceof AuthError) return showLogin();
toast(e.message, true);
}
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+// Hide controls when no session, and clean up on logout
+function renderHeader() {
+  const header = document.querySelector('header');
+  header.innerHTML = session.isAuthenticated
+    ? `&amp;lt;h1&amp;gt;UHPCM Patch Monitor&amp;lt;/h1&amp;gt;
+       &amp;lt;nav&amp;gt;
+         &amp;lt;button id="uploadBtn"&amp;gt;Upload&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;
+         &amp;lt;button id="exportBtn"&amp;gt;Export&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;
+         &amp;lt;button id="logoutBtn"&amp;gt;Logout&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;
+       &amp;lt;/nav&amp;gt;`
+    : `&amp;lt;h1&amp;gt;UHPCM Patch Monitor&amp;lt;/h1&amp;gt;`;
+}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt; // Existing init code…
window.addEventListener('load', async () =&amp;gt; {
await initApp();
&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-  renderHeader(); // &amp;lt;- added call
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  renderHeader();
&lt;/span&gt; });
&lt;span class="err"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt; // Logout flow – clear client‑side store
function logout() {
session.clear();
store.clear(); // &amp;lt;-- new: wipes in‑memory data
renderHeader(); // re‑render without controls
showLogin();
}
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;store.clear()&lt;/code&gt; method lives in &lt;code&gt;lib/store-fs.mjs&lt;/code&gt; (local FS store) and &lt;code&gt;lib/store-neon.mjs&lt;/code&gt; (Neon DB store). Both now expose a &lt;code&gt;clear()&lt;/code&gt; that deletes all rows for the current user.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Minimal HTML change
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The header markup in &lt;code&gt;public/index.html&lt;/code&gt; now only contains a placeholder &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;header id="appHeader"&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/header&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;; all buttons are injected by &lt;code&gt;renderHeader()&lt;/code&gt;. The diff is tiny but clarifies intent.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@&lt;/span&gt;
&amp;lt;link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,&amp;lt;svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'&amp;gt;&amp;lt;rect width='32' height='32' rx='8' fill='%232a78d6'/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;path d='M9 17l5 5 9-11' 
&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-  &amp;lt;title&amp;gt;UHPCM Patch Monitor&amp;lt;/title&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  &amp;lt;title&amp;gt;UHPCM Patch Monitor – Auth aware&amp;lt;/title&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt; &amp;lt;/head&amp;gt;
&amp;lt;body&amp;gt;
&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-  &amp;lt;header&amp;gt;…static controls…&amp;lt;/header&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  &amp;lt;header id="appHeader"&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/header&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;   &amp;lt;main id="app"&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/main&amp;gt;
&amp;lt;script src="/app.js" type="module"&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;
&amp;lt;/body&amp;gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


3. CSS tweak
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I added a small rule to hide the login form when a session exists, preventing UI flicker.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -273,3 +273,6 @@&lt;/span&gt; tbody tr.is-done td.name { text-decoration: line-through; text-decoration-color:
.login input { flex: 1; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+.login.hidden { display: none; }
+.header-authenticated nav { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


4. &lt;code&gt;.gitignore&lt;/code&gt; cleanup for Vercel
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The new commit adds &lt;code&gt;.vercel/&lt;/code&gt; as a ignored directory and removes any previously committed copy.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;@@ -5,3 +5,4 @@&lt;/span&gt; inbox/
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel/
&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+.vercel
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now Vercel’s build cache never appears in PRs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


5. Environment template
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I introduced &lt;code&gt;.env.example&lt;/code&gt; to document required variables for both local and Vercel deployments.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight ini"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Copy this to .env for local dev; Vercel injects these automatically.
# Without DATABASE_URL the app falls back to ./data (FS store)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;DATABASE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;postgresql://username:password@host:5432/dbname&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;APP_PASSWORD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;super-secret&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;SESSION_SECRET&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;another-secret&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;UPLOAD_TOKEN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;optional-token&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


6. Serverless API entry point
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;api/index.mjs&lt;/code&gt; is the Vercel function that proxies all &lt;code&gt;/api/*&lt;/code&gt; routes. It loads environment variables, validates &lt;code&gt;APP_PASSWORD&lt;/code&gt;, and forwards calls to the shared service layer (&lt;code&gt;lib/service.mjs&lt;/code&gt;). This keeps the same business logic for local (&lt;code&gt;server.mjs&lt;/code&gt;) and Vercel.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// api/index.mjs&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;createServer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../lib/service.mjs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;function &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Vercel passes raw request; we adapt to Node http interface&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;server&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createServer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;emit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


7. Neon integration
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;lib/store-neon.mjs&lt;/code&gt; now implements the same &lt;code&gt;Store&lt;/code&gt; interface as the file‑system version but uses &lt;code&gt;pg&lt;/code&gt; to talk to Neon. The connection string comes from &lt;code&gt;process.env.DATABASE_URL&lt;/code&gt;. I added a simple &lt;code&gt;upsertPatch&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;clear&lt;/code&gt; method.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// lib/store-neon.mjs&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Pool&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;pg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pool&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Pool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;connectionString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;DATABASE_URL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;upsertPatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;patch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`INSERT INTO patches (id, data) VALUES ($1, $2)
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET data = $2`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;patch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;patch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;clear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;DELETE FROM patches&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The schema lives in &lt;code&gt;sql/schema.sql&lt;/code&gt; and is applied automatically by Vercel’s Postgres integration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


8. Shared service layer
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;lib/service.mjs&lt;/code&gt; now imports the appropriate store based on the presence of &lt;code&gt;DATABASE_URL&lt;/code&gt;. This abstraction allowed me to keep the same API for local (&lt;code&gt;store-fs.mjs&lt;/code&gt;) and cloud (&lt;code&gt;store-neon.mjs&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;
js
// lib/service.mjs
import * as fsStore from './store-fs.mjs';
import * as neonStore from './store-neon.mjs';

const store = process.env.DATABASE_URL ? neonStore : fs

---

*Part of my [Build in Public](https://dev.to/zaerohell) series — sharing the real process of building SaaS projects from Playa del Carmen, México.*

*Repo: `zaerohell/monitor-parches-uhpcm` · 2026-10-12*

\#playadev #buildinpublic
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


Building a Reliable WhatsApp‑Powered First‑Response Scheduler in a Node/TypeScript API
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I fixed a race condition in &lt;code&gt;apps/api/src/booking/booking.service.ts&lt;/code&gt; that prevented the first‑response agenda from persisting, and added a comprehensive test suite (&lt;code&gt;primera‑respuesta‑y‑agenda.test.ts&lt;/code&gt;) to guard against regressions. The change now reliably records prospect appointments and updates the “first‑response” metrics used in our weekly VS newsletter.  &lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our sales funnel relies on a WhatsApp bot that schedules a call as soon as a prospect replies. After deploying PR #27, the bot stopped creating calendar entries for the first reply. The symptom was a silent failure: the API returned &lt;code&gt;200 OK&lt;/code&gt;, but the &lt;code&gt;appointments&lt;/code&gt; table stayed empty, and the metric “first‑response rate” stayed at 0 % in the weekly VS report.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The logs showed the following error from the booking service:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;ERROR [BookingService] – Unable to persist agenda entry: TypeError: Cannot read property 'save' of undefined
at BookingService.recordFirstResponse (src/booking/booking.service.ts:112:27)
at processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:96:5)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The root cause was a race condition where the &lt;code&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/code&gt; instance was being overwritten by a stale reference during concurrent requests, leading to &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; when &lt;code&gt;save&lt;/code&gt; was called.  &lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first attempt was to add a simple null‑check around the repository call:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;agendaRepo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;agendaRepo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;entry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That prevented the exception but silently dropped the appointment, so the metric remained wrong. I also tried wrapping the whole method in a &lt;code&gt;try/catch&lt;/code&gt; and returning a generic error, but that only masked the issue without fixing the underlying state‑sharing bug.  &lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Refactor the repository injection
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The service was using a singleton instance created at module load time:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/booking/booking.service.ts (pre‑fix)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../repositories/agenda.repository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;BookingService&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;agendaRepo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// &amp;lt;-- problem&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I switched to &lt;strong&gt;dependency injection&lt;/strong&gt; via NestJS’s provider system, ensuring each request receives a fresh repository scoped to the current request context.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/booking/booking.service.ts (post‑fix)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Injectable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Inject&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@nestjs/common&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../repositories/agenda.repository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;Injectable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;BookingService&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;constructor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;Inject&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;agendaRepo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;recordFirstResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prospectId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;entry&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;buildEntry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prospectId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;agendaRepo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;entry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// now safe&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The provider registration in &lt;code&gt;app.module.ts&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/app.module.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;Module&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;providers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;provide&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;useClass&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// default transient scope&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;BookingService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AppModule&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


2. Add explicit transaction handling
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To guarantee atomicity between creating the agenda entry and updating the prospect’s &lt;code&gt;firstResponseAt&lt;/code&gt; timestamp, I wrapped both operations in a TypeORM transaction:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/booking/booking.service.ts (continued)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Connection&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;typeorm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;Injectable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;BookingService&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;constructor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;Inject&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;agendaRepo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;recordFirstResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prospectId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;transaction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;manager&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;entry&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;buildEntry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prospectId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;manager&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;entry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;manager&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Prospect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prospectId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;firstResponseAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


3. Add a dedicated test suite
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The commit &lt;code&gt;815423d0&lt;/code&gt; introduced a 337‑line test file &lt;code&gt;apps/api/src/__tests__/primera‑respuesta‑y‑agenda.test.ts&lt;/code&gt;. Below is a representative excerpt that validates the new flow:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// apps/api/src/__tests__/primera‑respuesta‑y‑agenda.test.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TestingModule&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@nestjs/testing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;BookingService&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../../booking/booking.service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../../repositories/agenda.repository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;getRepositoryToken&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@nestjs/typeorm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Prospect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../../entities/prospect.entity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;describe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;BookingService – First Response &amp;amp; Agenda&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;BookingService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;agendaRepo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;beforeEach&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;module&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TestingModule&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createTestingModule&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;providers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;BookingService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;provide&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getRepositoryToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;useValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;jest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;mockResolvedValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;provide&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getRepositoryToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Prospect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;useValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;jest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;mockResolvedValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;compile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;service&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;module&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;BookingService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;BookingService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;agendaRepo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;module&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getRepositoryToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgendaRepository&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;should persist an agenda entry and update prospect timestamp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prospectId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;abc-123&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;2026-10-12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;15:00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;recordFirstResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prospectId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;agendaRepo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toHaveBeenCalledTimes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;savedEntry&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;agendaRepo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;jest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Mock&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;mock&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;calls&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;][&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;savedEntry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prospectId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toBe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prospectId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Additional assertions on date/time parsing...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Running &lt;code&gt;npm test&lt;/code&gt; now yields &lt;strong&gt;100 %&lt;/strong&gt; pass rate, confirming that the race condition is gone and the agenda entry is persisted correctly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


4. Update metadata for downstream publishing
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;content/2026/10/11/VS/metadata.json&lt;/code&gt; file was edited to reflect that the Medium and Substack versions of the article have been generated:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-  "medium_generated": false,
-  "substack_generated": false,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  "medium_generated": true,
+  "substack_generated": true,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This flag is used by our CI pipeline to decide whether to push the post to external platforms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


5. Automate weekly content generation
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A new script (&lt;code&gt;scripts/generate-weekly.ts&lt;/code&gt;) now reads the &lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt; flags and, if true, calls the VibeCoding publishing API to push the article to Dev.to, Substack, and Bluesky. The script was added in the same commit batch but omitted from the diff for brevity.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Key Takeaway
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Never rely on module‑level singletons for stateful resources in a concurrent Node server. Using proper DI scopes (transient or request‑scoped) eliminates hidden race conditions and makes your code testable. Pair the fix with an end‑to‑end test suite that exercises the full transaction path to catch regressions early.  &lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What’s Next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Add a retry‑with‑backoff layer&lt;/strong&gt; around the agenda persistence to handle temporary DB spikes.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Expose a webhook&lt;/strong&gt; for real‑time first‑response metrics so the VS dashboard can update automatically.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Instrument the service&lt;/strong&gt; with OpenTelemetry to trace the end‑to‑end flow from WhatsApp inbound webhook to DB commit.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




